HydraSDR third-party notices and provenance
===========================================

BirriaSDR
---------
HydraSDR is derived from BirriaSDR by Luigi C. and contributors. BirriaSDR's
MT7921 user-space SDR architecture, USB transport, receiver API, firmware and
related source provided the principal upstream foundation for this project.

The original BirriaSDR MIT copyright and permission notice is preserved
verbatim in LICENSES/BirriaSDR-MIT.txt. Individual inherited source files also
retain applicable upstream copyright/SPDX headers.

Upstream project:
https://github.com/luigifcruz/BirriaSDR

The exact-payload RX DMA framing correction includes work adapted from
BirriaSDR commit e9ea0e8a60f193e46eea60843869cc6508842682 by Yury MonZon,
under the same MIT license.

OpenWrt mt76
------------
src/usb.c and src/chips/mt7921_boot.c adapt portions of the BSD-3-Clause-Clear
user-space MT76 transport. The retained license text is in
LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-Clear.txt.

Source lineage:
https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/tree/c5a3bd91aa735b669618610d5f0ebfa5786845a6

Other research references
-------------------------
The high-level SDR API was informed by librtlsdr; no librtlsdr implementation
is incorporated.

The PHY gain-register layout was initially a research lead from w1700k-sdr and
was subsequently checked against the MT7961 target ROM and hardware. Its
calibration tables are not redistributed.

Mtk79ICAP was used as a comparative research source. No proprietary patch bytes
or vendor firmware from it are redistributed.

Dependencies and excluded artifacts
-----------------------------------
libusb is a separate LGPL-2.1-or-later dependency. HydraSDR does not embed
libusb, NumPy or Python, and the standalone release does not include vendor ROM
dumps, private vendor RAM/patch firmware, or private reverse-engineering
artifacts. No nonvolatile programming is implemented by the project.
